1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,755
Why would a free man sail home to a prison?

2
00:00:04,050 --> 00:00:10,900
Oregon. Sohan Singh Bhakna, a farmer from Punjab, stacks lumber in a sawmill.

3
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:17,100
Here he is taunted as a man from a slave country. The insult becomes his fuel.

4
00:00:17,150 --> 00:00:23,634
In 1913 the workers found the Ghadar Party, and choose him as its first president.

5
00:00:24,350 --> 00:00:31,500
He bows to no idol. As a Sikh, he bows only to the Guru’s word: stand against tyranny.

6
00:00:31,550 --> 00:00:36,300
A saint, Baba Kesar Singh, had taught him to live for others.

7
00:00:36,350 --> 00:00:42,646
So in 1914, as war begins, he sails for India to raise a revolt.

8
00:00:44,150 --> 00:00:49,779
The British are waiting. He is arrested as his ship reaches Calcutta.

9
00:00:49,850 --> 00:00:55,385
Sentenced to death, then to life, he spends 16 years in prison.

10
00:00:55,450 --> 00:00:59,862
He never bows. And he lives to see India free.
